---
kind: lore
id: farewell
title: The last two nights
---
/* The end of the week, side by side: Saturday night, then the three Sunday
endings at the bus shelter. One bundle so the ending conditions read as one
table (FINDINGS-0.23 N6 on what a bundle costs). */

<beat id="packing" on="slotStart" title="Saturday — Packing" priority="20" when="run.day == 6 && @night">
  ::bg{location="lantern_shop" time="night"}
  ::music{action="start" mood="wistful" volume="down"}
  ::auto{character="pell" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Your bag is half packed on the bed. The other half of it is somehow all over the shop.
  <match on="run.festivalWith">
    <when is="ines">
      @pell{code="0010" emotion="teasing"}: The library girl walked past the window twice today. Twice. The library is the other way.
    </when>
    <when is="theo">
      @pell{code="0020" emotion="teasing"}: There's a bundle of reed on the step with your name on it. Well. Not your name. "Qualified hands."
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @pell{code="0030"}: You'll come back next summer. Everyone says they won't and then they do.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
  @sol{code="0010" mono}: One more day.
  ::auto{character="pell" action="fadeOut"}
  ::music{action="fadeOut"}
</beat>

<beat id="ines" on="slotStart" title="Sunday — The almanac" priority="30" when="run.day == 7 && @night && has(run.festivalWith) && run.festivalWith == 'ines' && run.aff.ines >= 4">
  ::bg{location="marrow_bay_bus_shelter" time="night"}
  ::music{action="start" mood="tender" volume="down"}
  ::auto{character="ines" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
  @ines{code="0010" emotion="shy"}: The library's shut on Sundays. So technically I'm not working. So technically this is just — standing at a bus stop.
  @narrator{code="0010"}: She presses the 1962 tide almanac into your hands. Inside the cover, under someone's grandfather's handwriting, in hers: *Next summer. Wednesday afternoon. I'll put some aside.*
  @sol{code="0010"}: Ines —
  @ines{code="0020" emotion="happy"}: Don't. Say it next summer. It'll keep. Kozo holds when it's wet.
  ::auto{character="ines" action="fadeOut"}
  ::set{user.endings += 1}
  ::set{run.departed = true}
  ::end{reason="ending.ines"}
</beat>

<beat id="theo" on="slotStart" title="Sunday — Green reed" priority="30" when="run.day == 7 && @night && has(run.festivalWith) && run.festivalWith == 'theo' && run.aff.theo >= 4">
  ::bg{location="marrow_bay_bus_shelter" time="night"}
  ::music{action="start" mood="tender" volume="down"}
  ::auto{character="theo" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
  @theo{code="0010" emotion="neutral"}: Pell said six. It's five to. I ran.
  @narrator{code="0010"}: He holds out a bundle of green reed tied with fishing line.
  @theo{code="0020" emotion="shy"}: For next year's. Soak it the night before. Don't bend it dry. You know. You've got qualified hands.
  @sol{code="0010"}: Theo.
  @theo{code="0030" emotion="shy" when="holds('confided', ['theo'])"}: Dad would've liked you. He liked anyone who shut up and watched.
  @theo{code="0040" emotion="happy"}: The sea blushes in August too. Just so you know. Just — for planning purposes.
  ::auto{character="theo" action="fadeOut"}
  ::set{user.endings += 1}
  ::set{run.departed = true}
  ::end{reason="ending.theo"}
</beat>

<beat id="pell" on="slotStart" title="Sunday — The shop on Tern Street" priority="10" when="run.day == 7 && @night">
  ::bg{location="marrow_bay_bus_shelter" time="night"}
  ::music{action="start" mood="wistful" volume="down"}
  ::auto{character="pell" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
  @pell{code="0010" emotion="sad"}: Well. Seven days. That's a week, the way they used to make them.
  <match on="quest.festivalLantern.state">
    <when is="complete">
      @pell{code="0020" emotion="happy"}: Mrs Kaur says our lantern got furthest out. She's a liar, but she's a kind one.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @pell{code="0030"}: Next year there'll be a lantern. You'll see. I'll practise.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
  @pell{code="0040"}: Go on. The driver won't wait, he never has.
  @sol{code="0010" mono}: Through the back window, the shop sign on Tern Street, getting small. Then the headland. Then only the lighthouse.
  ::auto{character="pell" action="fadeOut"}
  ::set{user.endings += 1}
  ::set{run.departed = true}
  ::end{reason="ending.pell"}
</beat>
